{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>These are the statutes and the ordinances.</b> They are those written in the pericopes of \"And these are the ordinances\" and the pericope of \"On Mount Sinai.\"" "<b>Which HaShem gave between Himself and the children of Israel.</b> An allusion to the covenant of Mount Sinai. For after the Tabernacle was made and the Glory was in the Tent of Meeting, Moses did not ascend Mount Sinai. The pericope of valuations is also mentioned because it was stated on Mount Sinai, as it says at its end, and as the beginning of the book [Numbers] says: \"And YHWH spoke to Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, in the Tent of Meeting\" — in the book of Leviticus."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "The syntax of the final clause is compressed and the referent of באחרונה ('at its end') is ambiguous; rendered hyper-literally without resolving whether Ibn Ezra means the end of the valuations pericope or another textual boundary."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:56.688412368Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}